---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { release, site } from '../data/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<BaseLayout title="Download" description="Download the verified Windows x64 Inventatory prerelease from GitHub and read installation instructions.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro"><h1>Download Inventatory</h1><p class="lead">The Windows desktop application is available as a public beta. A scanner is not required to manage your inventory.</p></header>
    <section class="release-section" aria-labelledby="release-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Windows x64</p><h2 id="release-title">Inventatory {release.version}</h2><p class="release-status">{release.status} · Release candidate</p><p>This is a testing release. Read the release notes before updating an existing installation and make a backup of your inventory.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={release.package}>Download Windows x64 ZIP ↓</a><a href={release.url}>Release notes ↗</a></div><p class="meta checked">Release and package checked {release.checked}. <a href={site.releases}>Check GitHub for newer releases.</a></p></div>
      <aside><h3>Before you start</h3><ul><li>A Windows x64 PC.</li><li>A terminal with at least 100 × 30 cells.</li><li>A writable folder for inventory data.</li><li>A backup before replacing an existing installation.</li></ul><a href={url('/docs/getting-started/installation/')}>Installation and first-run guide →</a></aside>
    </section>
    <div class="download-notes section">
      <section><h2>Already installed?</h2><p>Use <strong>Settings → Updates</strong> in Inventatory. The updater shows release notes, downloads the package, verifies its published hashes, and hands off to the installer.</p><a href={url('/docs/desktop/settings/#software-updates')}>Read about application updates →</a></section>
      <section><h2>Scanner resources</h2><p>A public Scan R1 firmware release and assembly package have not been verified. Use the scanner documentation to understand the existing desktop integration and its setup requirements.</p><a href={url('/docs/scanner/status/')}>Hardware and firmware status →</a></section>
      <section><h2>Source code and license</h2><p>The desktop application is published under GPL-3.0-only. Build instructions and developer documentation live with the source.</p><a href={site.repository}>Open the application repository ↗</a></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .release-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-16); border-top: var(--border) solid var(--divider); padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-12); }
  .release-status { color: var(--warning); font: var(--text-sm)/1.5 var(--font-mono); margin-block: var(--space-3) var(--space-6); }
  .checked { margin-top: var(--space-6); } aside { padding-left: var(--space-8); border-left: var(--border) solid var(--divider); } aside ul { color: var(--secondary); }
  .download-notes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-8); }
  .download-notes h2 { font-size: var(--text-lead); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); } .download-notes a { display: inline-block; margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) { .release-section, .download-notes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-8); } aside { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; border-top: var(--border) solid var(--divider); padding-top: var(--space-6); } }
</style>
